A20. Dip. ~ RET
A21. Picnickers. ~ ANTS
A23. A cover-up agent. ~ TOUPEE
A25. A river that flows thru crossword puzzles. ~ YSER
A27. This'll put an end to abuse. ~ USE
A28. Any hostler could make his fortune here. ~ INN
A29. Egg plant. ~ HEN
A31. What Mussolini probably will never call his butler. ~ SMEDLEY
A35. Frogs' Paradise. ~ PAREE
A38. Back in the old days this clung round Grandpa of an evening. ~ CAPE
A40. What many an old Roman hen used to cackle over. ~ OVA
A41. The Constitution says men are born this way—but the Socialists claim they're born better. ~ EQUAL
A42. This escapes from the Senatorial gas pipes. ~ AIR
A43. Where there's a Suthin Cunnul there's this. ~ JULEP
A45. This holds the steering wheel on a speeding automobile. ~ NUT
A46. This is good for a whirl. ~ EDDY
